viewer: walk inwards from a first or last entry that fails to open

Opening the first or last entry walks on to the next one that opens when
it fails, as a directory's other files do once imagelist.adjacent lists
them. The walk's direction counted First as backward and Last as forward,
so a failed last entry walked past the end and wrapped to the first image,
and a failed first entry wrapped to the last. From the first it now walks
onwards, and from the last back.

--- a/src/viewer.cpp
+++ b/src/viewer.cpp
@@ -69,7 +69,8 @@
         next = il.get(nullptr, ImageList::Dir::First);
     }
 
-    const bool forward = dir != ImageList::Dir::First &&
+    // A failed end walks inwards: from the first onwards, from the last back.
+    const bool forward = dir != ImageList::Dir::Last &&
         dir != ImageList::Dir::Prev && dir != ImageList::Dir::PrevParent;
 
     while (true) {
